Source landscape: The 2023 Mexico conflict/force environment is primarily domestic rather than interstate: organized-crime violence, military and National Guard deployments, Ayotzinapa accountability, Nuevo Laredo killings, military budgets and procurement, civilian oversight, surveillance, disappearances, and migration-border operations. The source universe includes official presidential and military records, court decisions, congressional/audit material, UN/OAS/ICRC-related material, human-rights organizations, investigative journalism, academic/analytical reports, and favorable government narratives. Several records are post-2023 publications documenting 2023 events or outcomes. Search-result discovery was used only to identify candidates; no evidence claims or scores are assigned here.

